[Music]  I'm Wylie Dufresne and we are here at  Gustavus and coffee and waves or  Brooklyn we have 12 different doughnuts  that we serve right now different  flavors some are sugar summer glazed  I've come by my donut love honestly I  think my great-grandfather was a donut  maker in Central Falls Rhode Island and  I ate a lot of doughnuts as a kid and  for me it's about childhood about my  childhood memories tips that still  resonate with me today it's a pretty  standard profit we started with flour  baking powder and sugar in salt and  nutmeg we mix that all together we then  fold in our butter and then we add our  egg yolks and our milk we blend that  together into a batter we let that  batter rest for a period of time and  then we load that batter into the robot  the robot does a good job of dropping  the donut in a nice ring and it floats  downstream sort of in the spirit of the  lazy river at the halfway point it flips  them over for us and then once the  donuts come out and they've cooled a  little bit we blazing and we have about  11 different glazes that we use I think  when you look at our donuts you can  immediately say okay that's it let's do  some and it looks like these and our  flavors I think our flavors are are what  helps you realize you're having you know  one of our Delma  it's just something I want to do for a  long time I think it's a great  opportunity for creativity it's a great  up which you need to have some fun and  be playful and we tend to be sort of  endlessly tinkering with things and  tweaking and trying to make it better  today than it was yesterday  [Music]

